Fossify issue analysis
---------------------
The Messages #929 patch was informed by FossifyOrg/Messages issue #929 and
fatehiman's explanation/commit 44d2d3876088522785bb2f5d43b54226a6dce555.
It independently adds the selected-thread cancellation pattern already used
by Fossify; it does not incorporate the fork's broader lifecycle/sweep code.
The File Manager patch was informed by FossifyOrg/File-Manager issue #513
and the public Fossify Commons/File Manager source behavior. All patches
remain GPL-3.0 under this repository's license.
Messages lifecycle patches #927/#928 likewise acknowledge fatehiman's public
issue analysis and reference implementation 44d2d3876088522785bb2f5d43b54226a6dce555.
The implementation here uses synchronized per-Activity weak state, exact
provider-message scoping and original notification fallback, without the
fork's global notification sweep.

Contacts #327 acknowledges jeremiepose's issue diagnosis of missing merged
email/note display fields. Music Player #50 acknowledges the issue author
and Aga-C, knuxyl and aicode8000's album-art analysis and reproduction.
The focused implementations preserve source records and audio tags; the
Opus picture reader is an independent bounded read-only implementation.

Feeder #391
------------
The image-zoom patch targets Feeder 2.25.0 by Jonas Kalderstam and contributors,
GPL-3.0: https://github.com/spacecowboy/Feeder . The native linked-image callback
is preserved, and runtime bridge definitions refer to Feeder's shipped models,
image loader and coroutine ABI. The separate viewer and focused acceptance
fixtures are Penguin Patches code. No APK, signing key, Coil, Kotlin, Compose or
other runtime library is embedded in the repository or Feeder extension payload.

